WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.190 --> 00:00:03.023
- Come in.

00:00:04.107 --> 00:00:06.690
(door opening)

00:00:19.675 --> 00:00:20.508
- That it?

00:00:22.410 --> 00:00:24.010
Is that the welcoming committee?

00:00:26.280 --> 00:00:27.580
- What more is to be said?

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:32.627
- [Charles] How about
"thank you" or "well done"?

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.100
- If we all had to thank one another

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:37.160
every time we did anything in this family,

00:00:37.160 --> 00:00:38.360
we'd never get anywhere.

00:00:47.120 --> 00:00:49.010
- I've just been on a very challenging

00:00:49.010 --> 00:00:50.900
post-investiture tour of Wales.

00:00:50.900 --> 00:00:53.350
It went better than anyone expected.

00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:54.183
Thank you.

00:00:55.330 --> 00:00:57.810
- You were sent to Wales to show respect

00:00:57.810 --> 00:01:00.963
and heal divisions, not inflict
them on your own family.

00:01:02.389 --> 00:01:05.173
- I did nothing of the sort.

00:01:05.173 --> 00:01:06.550
- I've had the opportunity now

00:01:06.550 --> 00:01:09.070
to read the translation
of what you actually said

00:01:09.070 --> 00:01:10.493
and the inferences you made.

00:01:11.540 --> 00:01:14.480
The similarity between Wales'
suffering and yours was clear.

00:01:14.480 --> 00:01:16.543
- Was it?
- Unmistakable.

00:01:18.030 --> 00:01:18.863
- Only to you.

00:01:20.570 --> 00:01:21.920
- To all Wales, apparently.

00:01:27.010 --> 00:01:29.620
If this union is to
endure, then we must learn

00:01:29.620 --> 00:01:32.130
to respect each other's differences.

00:01:32.130 --> 00:01:34.782
Nobody likes to be ignored, to not be seen

00:01:34.782 --> 00:01:37.133
or heard or listened to.

00:01:39.100 --> 00:01:40.050
- Well, am I wrong?

00:01:41.120 --> 00:01:43.102
Isn't there a similarity
between my predicament

00:01:43.102 --> 00:01:44.113
and the Welsh?

00:01:45.460 --> 00:01:47.060
Am I listened to in this family?

00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.850
Am I seen for who and what I am?

00:01:49.850 --> 00:01:51.150
No.

00:01:51.150 --> 00:01:52.200
Do I have a voice?

00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:54.350
- Rather too much of
a voice for my liking.

00:01:55.670 --> 00:01:58.370
Not having a voice is something
all of us have to live with.

00:01:58.370 --> 00:02:01.560
We have all made sacrifices
and suppressed who we are.

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.500
Some portion of our natural
selves is always lost.

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:05.653
- That is a choice.

00:02:06.580 --> 00:02:08.610
- It is not a choice.

00:02:08.610 --> 00:02:09.573
It is a duty.

00:02:11.010 --> 00:02:13.270
I was a similar age to you
when your great-grandmother,

00:02:13.270 --> 00:02:15.540
Queen Mary, told me that to do nothing,

00:02:15.540 --> 00:02:18.410
to say nothing, is the hardest job of all.

00:02:18.410 --> 00:02:21.083
It requires every ounce
of energy that we have.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.773
To be impartial is not
natural, it's not human.

00:02:25.900 --> 00:02:28.520
People will always want
us to smile or agree

00:02:28.520 --> 00:02:32.520
or frown or speak and
the minute that we do,

00:02:32.520 --> 00:02:34.320
we will have declared a position,

00:02:34.320 --> 00:02:36.420
a point of view, and
that is the one thing,

00:02:36.420 --> 00:02:39.223
as a royal family, we
are not entitled to do,

00:02:40.113 --> 00:02:42.270
which is why we have
to hide those feelings,

00:02:42.270 --> 00:02:46.229
keep them to ourselves
because the less we do,

00:02:46.229 --> 00:02:49.190
the less we say or speak or agree or--

00:02:49.190 --> 00:02:50.023
- Think.

00:02:51.980 --> 00:02:55.873
Or breathe or feel or exist.

00:02:58.050 --> 00:02:58.883
- The better.

00:03:01.370 --> 00:03:02.760
- [Charles] Well, doing
that is perhaps not

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:04.360
as easy for me as it is for you.

00:03:05.890 --> 00:03:07.610
- Why?
- 'Cause I have

00:03:07.610 --> 00:03:08.864
a beating heart.

00:03:08.864 --> 00:03:12.410
(poignant music)

00:03:12.410 --> 00:03:13.243
A character.

00:03:15.656 --> 00:03:17.056
A mind and a will of my own.

00:03:18.580 --> 00:03:20.243
I am not just a symbol.

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:23.590
I can lead not just by wearing a uniform

00:03:23.590 --> 00:03:26.780
or by cutting a ribbon, but
by showing people who I am.

00:03:33.480 --> 00:03:35.313
Mummy, I have a voice.

00:03:38.380 --> 00:03:39.930
- Let me let you into a secret.

00:03:41.460 --> 00:03:43.123
No one wants to hear it.

00:03:48.058 --> 00:03:51.593
- Are you talking about the
country or my own family?

00:03:54.190 --> 00:03:55.023
- No one.

